,"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/catalog#write-the-intent","content":"the source: a recipe lane and step, or a mined ledger;"},"14":{"id":"/docs/corpus/catalog-12","page_id":"/docs/corpus/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/catalog#write-the-intent","content":"the variants to build, such as `p30-mainnet`, `p28-testnet` or `p30-mainnet-galexie`, and optionally mined variants beside the generated ones;"},"15":{"id":"/docs/corpus/catalog-13","page_id":"/docs/corpus/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/catalog#write-the-intent","content":"the focus: an operation of the step's transaction, or `{\"ledger\": true}` when the entry is about the ledger itself. A mined entry names its transaction by hash; the compiler never picks one;"},"16":{"id":"/docs/corpus/catalog-14","page_id":"/docs/corpus/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/catalog#write-the-intent","content":"the facts."},"17":{"id":"/docs/corpus/catalog-15","page_id":"/docs/corpus/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/catalog#compile-it","content":"The compiler takes the ledger bytes from a fresh `make generate` run (or from `mined/`) and finds the focus transaction. It resolves every fact into an exact JSON Pointer for that variant, and records size, sha256, provenance and change-order data. It needs the runs of `make generate`, for the base P30 mainnet variants also those of `make order-scan` (it ships the most frequent byte ordering), and the native reader (`make native`). A fact that doesn't hold fails the build, and so does a variant whose focus doesn't match the catalog's (a transaction where the catalog says ledger, or none where it names one): intent and outcome must agree before an entry exists."},"18":{"id":"/docs/corpus/catalog-16","page_id":"/docs/corpus/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/catalog#check-it","content":"`make verify` and `make oracle` check the built entries like any other. `make novelty` then fails if the new entry adds nothing another entry doesn't already hold."},"19":{"id":"/docs/corpus/catalog-17","page_id":"/docs/corpus/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/catalog#fact-addresses","content":"A fact names where it looks with `at`. The compiler resolves that address per variant, so one catalog file serves every protocol, network and flag profile."},"20":{"id":"/docs/corpus/catalog-18","page_id":"/docs/corpus/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/catalog#fact-addresses","content":"| `at`        | Resolves to                    |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `tx.result` | the focus transaction's result |","table":"table-0"},"21":{"id":"/docs/corpus/catalog-19","page_id":"/docs/corpus/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/catalog#fact-addresses","content":"| `at`             | Resolves to                       |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `tx.result_pair` | the result pair (hash and result) |","table":"table-0"},"22":{"id":"/docs/corpus/catalog-20","page_id":"/docs/corpus/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/catalog#fact-addresses","content":"| `at`             | Resolves to     |\n| ---------------- | --------------- |\n| `tx.fee_charged` | the fee charged |","table":"table-0"},"23":{"id":"/docs/corpus/catalog-21","page_id":"/docs/corpus/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/catalog#fact-addresses","content":"| `at`          | Resolves to                                                         |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tx.envelope` | the envelope in the transaction set, in any phase, stage or cluster |","table":"table-0"},"24":{"id":"/docs/corpus/catalog-22","page_id":"/docs/corpus/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/catalog#fact-addresses","content":"| `at`      | Resolves to            |\n| --------- | ---------------------- |\n| `tx.meta` | the transaction's meta |","table":"table-0"},"25":{"id":"/docs/corpus/catalog-23","page_id":"/docs/corpus/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/catalog#fact-addresses","content":"| `at`                                     | Resolves to                        |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `tx.fee_processing`, `tx.post_apply_fee` | the fee and post-apply fee changes |","table":"table-0"},"26":{"id":"/docs/corpus/catalog-24","page_id":"/docs/corpus/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/catalog#fact-addresses","content":"| `at`                                 | Resolves to                         |\n| ------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------- |\n| `op.meta`, `op.changes`, `op.events` | the focus operation inside the meta |","table":"table-0"},"27":{"id":"/docs/corpus/catalog-25","page_id":"/docs/corpus/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/catalog#fact-addresses","content":"| `at`     | Resolves to                                      |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `ledger` | the whole ledger: header, upgrades, evicted keys |","table":"table-0"},"28":{"id":"/docs/corpus/catalog-26","page_id":"/docs/corpus/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/catalog#fact-addresses","content":"A value may be `{\"$manifest\": \"contracts.kit2.CA1\"}`. It is then read from the run's own manifest, so a fact holds on every network even though contract ids differ by passphrase."},"29":{"id":"/docs/corpus/catalog-27","page_id":"/docs/corpus/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/catalog#fact-addresses","content":"<Callout title=\"Authoring aid\">`node tools/inspect.mjs <lane> <step> [variant]` reads a `make generate` run and prints the focus transaction's result and fee, and for each operation the kinds of its changes and its events.</Callout>"},"30":{"id":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53","page_id":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53","type":"page","content":"A payment of 9.5e15 stroops, above 2^53","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Corpus","Entries","Amounts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53"},"31":{"id":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53-0","page_id":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53","content":"An amount above 2^53 cannot be held exactly by a double: JavaScript numbers and float JSON parsers round it."},"32":{"id":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53-1","page_id":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53#the-shape","content":"The shape"},"33":{"id":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53-2","page_id":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53#variants","content":"Variants"},"34":{"id":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53-3","page_id":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53#what-a-correct-reader-returns","content":"What a correct reader returns"},"35":{"id":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53-4","page_id":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53#check-it-yourself","content":"Check it yourself"},"36":{"id":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53-5","page_id":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/entries/amount-payment-above-2-pow-53#check-it-yourself","content":"Entry id `amount.payment-above-2-pow-53` · compiled from `catalog/amount.payment-above-2-pow-53.json` · `entry.json`"},"37":{"id":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore","page_id":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore","type":"page","content":"A contract call restores an archived entry and overwrites it in one operation","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Corpus","Entries","Archival and restore"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore"},"38":{"id":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore-0","page_id":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore","content":"SorobanTransactionDataExt v1 marks readWrite[0] archived: the call restores it (restored changes for the entry and its TTL) and then updates it."},"39":{"id":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore-1","page_id":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore#the-shape","content":"The shape"},"40":{"id":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore-2","page_id":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore#variants","content":"Variants"},"41":{"id":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore-3","page_id":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore#what-a-correct-reader-returns","content":"What a correct reader returns"},"42":{"id":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore-4","page_id":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore#check-it-yourself","content":"Check it yourself"},"43":{"id":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore-5","page_id":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/entries/archival-automatic-restore#check-it-yourself","content":"Entry id `archival.automatic-restore` ·