pplies the classic phase first, then the Soroban phase, each in an order shuffled by the hash of the whole set (TxSetFrame.cpp ApplyTxSorter)."],[1530,"The transfer argument is M(bob, 2^64-1). The event names bob's G address in topics and carries the ID as to_muxed_id (u64) in a data map instead of a bare i128."],[1506,"The trustline is found by matching a change \"in any order\": an indexer must never depend on the order of changes within an operation."],[1947,"The two recipe sets"],[2365,"The two runs of a pair are compared ledger by ledger. They must be byte-identical, or identical after normalising. Normalising sorts the order of changes within an operation and zeroes the diagnostic `invoke_time_nsecs` timing value."],[2613,"The types are at the crate root in 30.0.0 (a first try with `stellar_xdr::curr::…` did not compile). From an empty folder, on cargo 1.98.1:"],[2417,"The unbounded walk is wallet-backend#820: today's deepest tree (245 levels) survives it, so it is hardening. XDRProof's patch bounds it at depth 256 and 4,096 nodes and stops, counted and logged, instead of failing; it is offered on #820. The three Blend sites are the shape wallet-backend fixed in its SEP-41 processor (#756), not reachable today. Both patches are in `linter/patches/`; with them, wallet-backend's own build, vet and tests pass."],[1505,"The variants are **generated** by a standalone stellar-core v30.0.0 at protocols 30 and 28. On most of them the order of the operation's changes is not stable between core processes, so those pin an order-normalised hash and list every raw ordering seen."],[14,"the variants to build, such as `p30-mainnet`, `p28-testnet` or `p30-mainnet-galexie`, and optionally mined variants beside the generated ones;"],[1630,"The verdict is read from state: the ingest cursor and the stored signer's length. See Replay."],[2513,"The wallet-backend adapter builds each commit in a pinned Go image, runs TimescaleDB 2.28.2 as its compose file does, copies each session's